# Production environment variables must be configured securely in your hosting provider (e.g. Vercel Project Settings).
# Never commit real database URLs, secrets, passwords, or payment keys to Git.
#
# Required production variables:
# - DATABASE_URL (PostgreSQL connection string, pooled if using serverless)
# - SESSION_SECRET (cryptographically random string, >= 32 chars)
# - RAZORPAY_KEY_ID / NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID / RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET / RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# - DIRECT_URL (PostgreSQL unpooled connection string for Prisma migrations)
# - AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3 / AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY / AWS_REGION (Neon Object Storage `assets` + `rescues` buckets)
#   OR BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN (Vercel Blob storage for public & private images)
# - UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN (distributed serverless rate limiting)
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL (canonical production origin)
